## Conversation
Started from a GLM-5.2 eval-history question, narrowed to baseline (zai FP8) vs
our NVFP4 self-quant. User then hit a vLLM ValueError on `layer_types` in
staging and asked whether it was an engine or checkpoint fault, then what newer
transformers versions were usable. User laid out a 4-repo chain: ml-containers
(this bump) -> infr (rebuild dynamo-vllm) -> cks-inference-deploy
(runtime-engines.yaml) -> fix the gh-stack over PRs 1550/1552. Tag alexeldeib on
every step. This commit is step 1 only.

## Actions
Probed three cw-infr-oci/dynamo-vllm images (v2.22.0, v2.26.0, v2.29.1) as pods
on cw598e-use15 using the `infr-image-pull` secret in `default`. Read
ALLOWED_LAYER_TYPES, dependency metadata, and ran the validator standalone.
Downloaded transformers wheels 5.9.0-5.14.1 from PyPI and grepped the allowlist,
then load-tested nvidia/GLM-5.2-NVFP4's real config.json under each version via
`uv run --with transformers==X`. Edited only the pin + its comment bullet.

## Errors & Mistakes
Initially concluded from wheel-grepping that 5.13+ REGRESSED (the global
ALLOWED_LAYER_TYPES shrinks 15 -> 10 entries and loses
deepseek_sparse_attention). Wrong: actually loading the config under 5.13.1 and
5.14.1 succeeds, so GlmMoeDsaConfig declares its own permitted types there.
Grepping the constant is not a valid test; load the config instead.

Also mis-inferred earlier that staging served our smoke checkpoint and that
`raw/coreweave/GLM-5.2-NVFP4/v1` might hold NVIDIA weights. The init container
showed the real path: `s3://infr-cwc38d/raw/nvidia/GLM-5.2-NVFP4/aec724e8...`.
No prefix mixup exists.

## Dead Ends
Expected `modelopt[hf]`'s `>=4.56,<5.10` pin to block this bump, as it did in
our quantize image. modelopt is NOT installed in the serving image at all, so it
imposes nothing. Also could not read the deployed config from S3
(infr-cwc38d 403 with the cw4637 profile) or exec into the crashing pod
(`pods/exec` denied) -- fetched the config from HuggingFace by revision instead,
and it diffed zero keys against our mirrored copy.

## Hints for Future Agents
The floor is transformers 5.11.0, which is exactly the version NVIDIA used to
serialize the checkpoint. First drafted as 5.12.1, then the user said "bump to
the latest that we can get away with", so it landed on the 5.14.1 tip -- checked
safe because every 5.14.1 requirement is already satisfied in-image with zero
transitive upgrades (safetensors sits exactly at its new >=0.8.0 floor). This
bump is UNVALIDATED against a real forward pass -- only
config construction was tested -- so a serve smoke test on Gemma 4 MTP, Kimi
K2.5/K3 and DeepSeek-V4 is the gate before promotion, since those are the other
models whose reasons are recorded in the same comment block.

Two lower-scope workarounds exist and may be preferable short-term: repoint the
deployment at `raw/coreweave/GLM-5.2-NVFP4/v1` (our smoke checkpoint, which
omits layer_types and serves today on eu-n-04a under v2.26.0), or strip
`layer_types` from config.json at the model-upload step. Both were verified.

## Codebase Discoveries
The image chain is ml-containers/vllm-tensorizer -> infr/images/vllm/Dockerfile
line 28 (`FROM ghcr.io/coreweave/ml-containers/vllm-tensorizer:<mlc-sha>-<vllm-sha>-cuda13.2.1-ubuntu24.04`)
-> cw-infr-oci/dynamo-vllm:vX.Y.Z -> cks-inference-deploy
config/values/runtime-engines.yaml `<vllm-ver>+crwv.<n>`. The ml-containers
commit sha is embedded in the base tag, so this commit's sha must reach infr.

All dynamo-vllm images through the newest (v2.29.1) shipped transformers 5.9.0 --
the version was not pinned by any dependency, just whatever resolved.

